id: time-freeze
name: Time Freeze
uaType: magical
prerequisite: Magic Score 8+, 2+ Skill Ranks in Use Magic
tpCost: 40
type: instant
actionCost: 0
kiCostPerBaseTier: 14
# "Immediately begin a Frozen Turn" - its 2 Actions kept on its user, spent in place of their own (combat.mjs
# frozenTurnOf); what may and may not be used during it refused where Maneuvers are (use-maneuver.mjs permitted, the
# Respond dialog, out of sequence); everyone else under the Frozen in Time mark; ended when both are spent or from its
# card (chat.mjs postTimeFreeze, endFrozenTurn). Applying Energy Charges through Traits during it is the table's.
# Passive: "You are not affected by the usual rules during another Character's Frozen Turn" - whoever has it is left out.
timeFreeze: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  An Instant Frozen Turn of 2 Actions: Standard Maneuvers only, no Ki Wager; everyone else's Defense Value 2(bT) and
  Perception 2 lower, and no Counter, Instant or Out-of-Sequence Maneuvers.
text: >
  Time Freeze: You can momentarily stop time for everyone else, allowing you to do as you please.
  –Ability Type: Magical
  –Prerequisites: Magic Score 8+, 2+ Skill Ranks in Use Magic
  –TP Cost: 40
  –KP Cost: 14(bT)
  –Maneuver Type: Instant
  –Action Cost: N/A
  –Minions: N/A
  –Passive Bonus: You are not affected by the usual rules during another Character’s Frozen Turn.
  –Effect: Immediately begin a Frozen Turn. A Frozen Turn is a unique Turn in which you have 2 Actions to use during this
  Turn, and the Turn ends when both of those Actions are used (you cannot use any other Actions you possess during a
  Frozen Turn).

  During a Frozen Turn you can only use Standard Maneuvers and cannot Ki Wager, use Instant or Out-of-Sequence Maneuvers,
  use Combat Recovery, use the Power Up Maneuver, the Energy Charge Maneuver, apply Energy Charges to Attacking Maneuvers
  through the effects of Traits, use any Special Maneuvers that target another Character, or use any Unique Abilities.

  During a Frozen Turn, other Characters cannot use Counter Maneuvers, Instant Maneuvers, or Out-of-Sequence Maneuvers
  (except Surges). Additionally, their Defense Value is reduced by 2(bT) and their Perception Skill Bonus is reduced by 2.
